There are two types of exceptions.
1) Checked exceptions: These are the exceptions which inherit the exception class directly. These exceptions need to be handled immediately as the compiler begins
to give redlines under the critical code, so we came to know that these lines of code are going to give exception even before the execution of the program.
This code need to be put under try and catch block before proceeding. 

2) Unchecked exceptions: These are the exceptions which inherit the runtime class. These exceptions need to be handled but not immediately as the compiler doesn't 
give any redline under the critical code. We came to know about the exception only after the execution of the code. Then we can put this critical code in try-catch
block to handle it.
